.git
node_modules
build
dist
user-data
data
backups
images
docs

# The host's own addresses. Compose reads .env from the host at run time, so the
# image never needs a copy, and an image layer is as copyable as a commit. Bun
# also auto-loads .env from the working directory before it runs anything, and a
# baked-in copy stopped it dead: `bun` exited 1 with no output at all, which took
# the client build down with it.
.env
.env.*

# This install's own port and folders, written beside the app on its first run.
# Compose sets CHUNGUS_HOST and CHUNGUS_DATA_DIR, which outrank the file, but
# nothing sets CHUNGUS_PORT - so a baked-in copy is the one thing left that can
# move the listener, and under host networking there is no port mapping to
# correct it. The container writes its own on first start; that is the copy that
# should win.
chungushub.config.json

# This checkout's own notes and tooling. CLAUDE.md says of itself that it never
# deploys, and `COPY . .` was quietly making that false.
CLAUDE.md
.claude

# `svelte-kit sync` runs inside the image, so a host-generated copy is never read
# - and one generated on Windows carries absolute host paths.
.svelte-kit
